# oodar version and compat contract
#
# Format: NAME=MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH[-PRERELEASE]
# Bump MAJOR: incompatible ABI change (consumers must rebuild against the new C symbols)
# Bump MINOR: backwards-compatible feature (consumers continue to link unchanged)
# Bump PATCH: backwards-compatible bug fix
#
# oodar is the Gen 1 host substrate for compiled openOODA binaries. The
# runtime ABI is the set of oo_* symbols exported by the per-subdir
# .c files. Per RULES.oot §1.21, a runtime ABI break is a Floor (MAJOR)
# bump; a feature addition is a Thrust (MINOR) bump; a bug repair is a
# Patch (PATCH) bump.
# The api_surface field is a structural check: the loader asserts the
# oodar repo ships exactly the declared count of public .c files
# (counted recursively across all 6 per-domain subdirs).
# The release_tag field is the assertion of the current shipping version;
# it must match the most recent git tag. See RULES.oot §1.24
# and rfcs/0006-versioning-and-release-protocol.oot.

oodar=3.2.3
release_tag=3.2.3
ooda=2.10.0
ooda_max=2.99.0
api_surface=90
# Note: api_surface counts all .c files that ship in v3.2.3
# (distributed across 6 per-domain subdirs: core, sec, fs, net, hw, app).
# v2.0.0 removed app/actor/cycle.c (zero callers, Bacon-Rajan
# cycle detection). v2.3.0 moved dudect_c_native.c and
# oo_hip_so_smoke.c from pqc/ and gpu/ to qa/ (test utilities that
# the file split surfaced as a natural cleanup). v3.1.0 removed 7
# dead/placeholder files and merged the dead JSON/python code in
# symmetric/crypto.c; net change: 94 → 90 .c files.
# The public ABI count is the count of distinct .c files in the
# repo, excluding build/host artifacts, qa/ tests, scripts/, and
# the umbrella oodar.c itself.
#
# v2.0.0 is a Floor break from v1.0.1. The audit closed 4 cap-gating
# gaps (oo_alloc/free/write_int/read_int/checkpoint/rollback and all
# oo_weak_*/oo_control_block_* mutators now require caps). The 22
# crypto_*_internal primitives are no longer in the public oodar.h;
# in-tree callers use sec/crypto/crypto_internal.h. See CHANGES.md
# for the full migration notes (what changed, what consumers must
# update, what did not change, the symbol signatures table).
#
# v3.0.0 is a Floor break from v2.2.0. The audit pass 3 / v2.1.0
# residuals converged on a single remaining gap: the 4 cap-free
# public mutator families. v3.0.0 closes them all in one Floor
# break. 8 public symbols gain a long long cap first arg and
# require the appropriate cap token. One new cap (MetricsCap) is
# introduced at bit 0x800 (the v2.1.0 AUDIT bit position, which
# had been reserved since v2.1.0 for exactly this kind of future
# re-introduction). The cap system grows from 25 to 26 tokens
# (22 implemented inline in sec/cap/caps.c + 4 split across
# core/mem/alloc.c, app/xlang/ffi_sec.c, fs/os/time_rand.c + the
# new metrics in sec/cap/caps.c). The entropy buffer grows from
# 175 to 184 bytes to fit the 8 new bytes for g_tok_metrics. The
# umbrella .o size is +1552 bytes (v2.2.0 = 386952, v3.0.0 = 388504;
# the new cap state + 8 require calls + 8 new function signatures
# in oodar.h outweigh the small rebalances). Consumers must
# rebuild. See CHANGES.md "v3.0.0" for the full signature-change
# table and the consumer migration notes.
#
# v2.3.0 is a Patch bump from v3.0.0 (per the v2.x version line for
# cleanup-only releases). The 256-line file cap is now enforced across
# all .c/.h files. 17 files over 256 lines were split into 60+ files
# across 9 new sub-dirs (hw/gpu/gpu/, types/, sec/cap/, sec/crypto/{aead,
# symmetric}/, sec/landlock/{landlock,sandbox}/, sec/pqc/{mlkem,mldsa,
# pq_sig}/, core/mem/arena_*, core/list/list_*, app/actor/actor_*). The
# public ABI is unchanged: every oo_* symbol keeps its v3.0.0 signature.
# The split is purely organizational — the runtime is byte-equivalent
# at the ABI level. Two algorithm-internal files (mldsa_internal.c 627
# lines, mlkem_internal.c 460 lines) remain over 256 by design: the
# FIPS 203/204 NTT + sampling + polynomial arithmetic are tightly
# coupled, and splitting them would fragment the algorithm without a
# functional boundary. See CHANGES.md "v2.3.0" for the full split
# manifest.
#
# v3.1.0 is a Floor break from v3.0.0. The round-4 deep-dive audit
# (6 lenses: zero trust, REDTEAM, power law, systems, OCap, Blue Ocean)
# found 4 CRITICAL fail-open security bugs and 5 HIGH/MED boundary
# violations. v3.1.0 closes all 4 CRITICALs in one Floor break:
#   1. GPU cap shadow: oo_gpu_hip_try_launch_dispatch previously
#      shadowed cap with 0, breaking every GPU call (REDTEAM + OCap).
#   2. time_rand.c LCG fallback: getentropy(3) failure previously
#      fell back to a predictable LCG (direct cap forge, OCap).
#   3. crypto.c LCG fallback: g_cg_sign_key had the same issue
#      (direct seal/verify forge, OCap).
#   4. oo_cap_attenuate bitmask subset: the API is missing the
#      Rule 2 check; deferred to v3.2.0 Floor break (audit said
#      separate Floor; documented with TODO).
# Plus 2 MED fixes: oo_bind_udp now correctly uses BindCap (matching
# the TCP path), and alloc.c closed a signed-overflow window in the
# ambient-quota check. Plus 7 dead/placeholder file removals (the
# power-law long tail) and the move of app/telemetry/event.{c,h} to
# core/event/ (resolving the sec/-depending-on-app/ boundary
# violation). api_surface 94 → 90. See CHANGES.md "v3.1.0" for the
# full audit-fix table.
